{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03YB", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-smooth}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:71a9522a6c9ff75c964aabb4eb11ae36ed56145dd9a7a7f36034c23892802c19", "source_text": "Smooth topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a968946b4d12f92a373bca211666d513dc16668d2222092407ec47a0d13f4615", "unit_id": "tag:03YB:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YB", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-section-smooth}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7363adcde87a6cfcae313587b2971257316b5456701ab220ac1c0b900c8cda7e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss the notion of a smooth covering of\nalgebraic spaces, and we define the big smooth site of an\nalgebraic space. Please compare with\nTopologies, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:31f655274c277fd4db9cd93f4f406a8ba63f545be1b9dc78cf61f8a9df55d4d6", "unit_id": "tag:03YB:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03YB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f_i$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n|X| = \\bigcup\\nolimits_{i \\in I} |f_i|(|X_i|),\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-smooth-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e76fae56c3226e3151fabee0092a70b466b5acf08f6f31c1ff32db92d85286f7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:55ea071ab33fb025ae011a89e7bae0d76a7b75fabcd3b8bfd519a7d0775fe1b4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>smooth covering of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family of morphisms\n<MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nsuch that each <MATH_0007> is smooth\nand such that\n<MATH_0008>\ni.e., the morphisms are jointly surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fa76ef817ae04d2861d746ac8a744602d13c360f850ae826005a0205d5903fc0", "unit_id": "tag:041C:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-definition-smooth-covering}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:471134057d0984d44af5a155ac2d0e8da290e691491a26f5be3167e4b5c64d48", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1116077311bb8d3177d0b23bd7ca7921129b39a139a0d9038a7f8ed0451fb167", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is exactly the same as\nTopologies, Definition <REF_0001>.\nIn particular, if <MATH_0001> and all the <MATH_0002> are schemes, then we recover the\nusual notion of a smooth covering of schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:24516dd9c255596140a09ea5f48e7850c100ab03df158f001936054b246a12fc", "unit_id": "tag:03YB:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03YB", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:925a966340ae93e6bb49ae2754015e7d97424d93a595ba3de76760319491f38f", "source_text": "Any <ACCENT_0001>tale covering is a smooth covering, and a fortiori,\nany Zariski covering is a smooth covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:12b05784c61bce7da3cced8d995a914a6d48f1babaaff00c39baf2fa092a0163", "unit_id": "tag:0DFA:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03YB", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-etale-smooth}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-zariski-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1256479f31ca35a09f92a1d4d636936f2f09b9e75276976a888ddf28c4937bbb", "source_text": "This is clear from the definitions, the fact that an\n<ACCENT_0001>tale morphism is smooth\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>), and\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e91e66f9794664ddef65f13e871f5ea56b4c2ea6d254d70e7d742c6c79f3e6d5", "unit_id": "tag:0DFA:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03YB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{X' \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$i$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0012": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{X' \\times_X X_i \\to X'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e3d9a30bc295880eafea81ddede5c59549b2394c91422582e284bba1fee4680", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c1225b1fb9b5d1a7f0b31008ccbd0042168b192807ff0540ca96e39cb0d6662b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0004> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0005>\nis a smooth covering of <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0007> is a smooth covering and for each\n<MATH_0008> we have a smooth covering <MATH_0009>, then\n<MATH_0010> is a smooth covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0011> is a smooth covering\nand <MATH_0012> is a morphism of algebraic spaces then\n<MATH_0013> is a smooth covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ba2bb19f9ddc682cddee96b64a0ad780b08fcdd46a6abc0954e21696db08d0cb", "unit_id": "tag:041D:statement"}
